# CODEOWNERS -- who must approve a change to what.
#
# Written as "everything is the founder's, except the folders builds work in".
# Listing only the files to protect is how the earlier drafts kept missing some
# -- the lock file, the loop's own code, a conftest.py beside the package --
# so this file is turned round: a catch-all first, then the carve-outs.
#
# GitHub's rules this relies on (read fresh at build time, 18 Nov 2026):
#   * the LAST matching pattern wins, so broad rules go first and the
#     carve-outs below them;
#   * a pattern with NO owners removes ownership for that path;
#   * the copy that governs a pull request is the one on the pull request's
#     BASE branch, so editing this file inside a pull request never changes who
#     is asked to review that same pull request;
#   * patterns are gitignore-style minus three features: no "!" negation, no
#     "[a-z]" ranges, no escaped "#". Matching is case-sensitive.
#
# UNTIL B05 THIS FILE HAS NO FORCE: nothing requires a code owner's review yet,
# and every session acts as the founder. B05 switches on the rulesets that make
# it binding, and then attacks them.

